1652	// refuseSharedInode rejects an open managed target that is a HARD link.
1653	//
1654	// Every other guard here reasons about a path, and a hard link has no path to
1655	// reason about. `ln .git/config CLAUDE.md` gives git's config a second name in
1656	// the working tree: it resolves to "CLAUDE.md", carries no `.git` component, and
1657	// Lstat reports an ordinary regular file, so PathLandsInGitDir cannot see it.
1658	// Writing the managed block through that name appends to git's own config —
1659	// exactly the corruption the git-directory refusal exists to prevent, reached by
1660	// a route it does not cover. Measured before this guard: `init-agents` exited 0
1661	// and `.git/config` was rewritten.
1662	//
1663	// The rule is link count rather than "is it inside .git", because the handle
1664	// cannot be asked where else its inode is named. That means it also refuses a
1665	// hard link to a harmless file. An instruction file with a second name is
1666	// vanishingly rare, sharing one is what the DOCUMENTED alias (a symlink) is for,
1667	// and the failure mode on the other side is silent corruption of the repository
