1676		// this command must not write. Hard-linking two managed instruction files
1677		// together is documented and supported, so the question is not "is this
1678		// file linked" but "is every one of its names a managed target".
1679		//
1680		// Counting is what answers that without being able to enumerate an inode's
1681		// names: if as many managed targets share this inode as the inode has
1682		// names, then all of its names are accounted for and all of them are ours.
1683		// One unaccounted name means some other path — `.git/config`, a hook —
1684		// reaches the same bytes, and the write must be refused.
1685		accounted := uint64(0)
