1687			// The entry must be a HARD LINK to count, and a symlink is not one.
1688			//
1689			// Only real directory entries contribute to an inode's link count, so
1690			// counting a symlink alias inflates `accounted` without inflating
1691			// `links` and hands back exactly the permission this guard exists to
1692			// withhold. Measured before this check: CLAUDE.md hard-linked to
1693			// .git/config (2 names) plus AGENTS.md symlinked to CLAUDE.md counted 2
1694			// managed names against 2 links, so init-agents exited 0 and rewrote
1695			// git's config. Sharing one instruction file through a SYMLINK is the
1696			// documented alias and stays supported; it simply is not evidence about
1697			// who else holds a hard link.
